  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5151",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple pathways leading to NCI-H82, with the most direct route involving A704, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18. This suggests a potential mechanism where Mollicellin N modulates A704, which in turn influences the activity of palmarumycin CP18, ultimately affecting NCI-H82. Complementary evidence shows that Mollicellin N also targets Leukocyte common antigen, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, further reinforcing the idea that Mollicellin N exerts its effects through diverse molecular interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with the core mechanism likely involving the modulation of A704 or its downstream targets. The evidence supports a role for Mollicellin N in influencing NCI-H82 through multiple, interconnected molecular pathways, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
